From: perf session 2026-09-11
Subject: [PATCH 0031] wasm64: scope Asyncify instrumentation to a coroutine-stack allowlist

The emscripten fiber coroutine backend unwinds the whole C stack at a
switch, so every frame that can be live at a switch must be Asyncify-
instrumented.  The build did this with -sASYNCIFY_REMOVE=tcg_qemu_tb_exec
(instrument everything except the interpreter).  Because the invoke_*
setjmp/longjmp wrappers and indirect calls pull almost everything into
the reachability set, ~21000 functions (17 MB of the 45 MB wasm) ended up
instrumented, and on the wasm64 backend that is ~25 % of the early-boot
vCPU time (Module/Instance-adjacent C code, helpers, translation) plus a
45 MB download.

The wasm64 backend runs guest code as JIT'd per-TB modules (addFunction),
not through tcg_qemu_tb_exec, so almost none of the instrumentation is on
a real switch path.  Replace REMOVE with -sASYNCIFY_ONLY=@asyncify-only.txt:
instrument ONLY the functions captured on an actual switch stack.  The
list was built with QEMU_COSTACK=1 (added to util/coroutine-wasm.c: log
each distinct JS/wasm stack at a switch) over a full pmb887x boot, rw
flash writes and shutdown, plus name-pattern families (block layer, aio,
coroutine, main loop, emscripten runtime).  Two prerequisites make the
list closed:

  - hw/arm/pmb887x/flash-blk.c: a writable-flash store ran blk_pwrite()
    (a block coroutine) from the vCPU thread's MMIO write handler, whose
    JIT'd TB frame + invoke_* wrapper can never be instrumented.  Defer
    the write to a main-loop bottom half (coalescing adjacent ranges);
    the storage array already holds the latest bytes, and a vm-state
    change handler flushes on stop.
  - util/coroutine-wasm.c: mark the vCPU thread (qemu_coroutine_forbid_
    current_thread) so a switch there aborts loudly instead of derailing.

wasm64-only (scripts/build-qemu-wasm64.sh overrides the shared cross
file): the TCI dist's hot path IS tcg_qemu_tb_exec, and the onlylist
regressed it +26 % (interleaved idlebench, both orders), so the TCI dist
keeps ASYNCIFY_REMOVE.

Measured (dist-jit, idlebench --runs 2 interleaved vs the session base):
wasm 45.1 MB -> 27.8 MB; tIdle 40.3 -> 33.2 s (-18 %); t0.5G 29.6 -> 24.0
(-19 %); early phase t0.1G 5.4 -> 3.3 (-39 %).  Gates: op-suite native
JIT+TCI 1156/1156 byte-identical; wasm64 lockstep 250e6 serial+regs
identical; boots to the idle screen (Chromium).

